# Public spec vs author-only notes

**Rule Rev.2** — 2026-09-13 (common)

The public specification is **English**. Author-only notes may be **Japanese**.
Do not merge the two.

## Public spec

- Current behaviour, invariants, schemas, Help checklist
- Measured performance (when the project has a gate)
- Factual product decisions (licence, “we do not sell”)
- Privacy policy and published scan **results** (not vendor-process essays)
- No Plan table, Ship memos, or future-vision essays
- Bug-fix behaviour stays public when it ships

Tone: professional and specific. No first-person asides.

## Author-only (`private_spec.md` and other `private_*`)

- Plan essays, QA checklists, leftover Ship tables
- Motivation, location, tax / bank / funding eligibility
- Discarded-idea diaries and “why I chose this”
- Competitor research and price tables
- Maintainer release / handoff checklists
- Pre-public version history (DialKey: anything before **1.0.0**). From the
  first public edition onward, keep per-version **product** facts in the
  public spec. Do not list earlier private builds there

When asked to record such a note, write **only** the private file.
When a public paragraph sounds like the list above, move it and leave a fact.

## Do not

- Commit `private_*` or copy its wording into Help / the docs site / the public spec
- Put shipped behaviour only in the private file — product facts stay public

---

## DialKey overlay

**Overlay Rev.2** — 2026-09-13

Public surfaces (`docs/spec.md`, README, docs site, Help, committed rules)
start at **1.0.0**. Do not add `0.x` version tables, ship memos, or
`docs/Old/`.

| Public | Not public |
|---|---|
| Behaviour §1–13, §10 n=10 for **1.0.0+**, MIT, VT **results**, one language-pack paragraph | `.cursor/rules/private_*` (Japanese OK): `private_spec.md`, `private_RELEASE.md`, `private_HANDOFF.md`, `private_stamp.md`, `private_spec_v1.9.md`, `private_appendix-changelog-phases-archive.md` |
| No Stream Deck / QMK / price table | Competitor tables |
| No pre-1.0 changelog | Local `docs/Old/` (gitignored) — same class as `private_*` |

Git **history** on a public repo still shows old commit messages (folder
last-commit on GitHub). That is not the product spec. Do not rewrite
history unless the user asks.

Do not edit `private_*` except `private_spec.md` when moving author notes out of the public spec.
